searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs","doc":"Locale-aware HTML form input components.\n\nThe first component is `Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1`\n— a locale-aware plain-number input. The library is structured\nso additional locale-aware inputs (percentages, ratios,\ndurations, dimensions, …) can be added under the same\n`Localize.Inputs.Components` namespace over time.\n\nThe package ships three layers:\n\n1. **Headless** — `Localize.Inputs.Parser`,\n   `Localize.Inputs.Formatter`, `Localize.Inputs.Validator`,\n   `Localize.Inputs.Locale`. Pure Elixir, no Phoenix\n   dependency. Useful from JSON APIs or non-LiveView projects.\n\n2. **Phoenix integration** — `Localize.Inputs.Components`\n   (HEEx components) and `Localize.Inputs.Changeset` (Ecto\n   helpers).\n\n3. **JS hook** — `priv/static/localize_inputs.js` wraps\n   [AutoNumeric](https://autonumeric.org/) for live formatting,\n   cursor preservation, paste sanitisation. Drop-in for\n   `Phoenix.LiveView` hooks.\n\nA web-based visualizer is included for local development at\n`Localize.Inputs.Visualizer` — see that module for the\nconfig gate.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick examples - Localize.Inputs","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"1.234,56\", locale: :de)\n    {:ok, Decimal.new(\"1234.56\")}\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number(Decimal.new(\"1234.56\"), locale: :en)\n    \"1,234.56\"","ref":"Localize.Inputs.html#module-quick-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.version/0","doc":"Returns the installed package version as a string.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.html#version/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.version/0","doc":"* The version string declared in `mix.exs`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.html#version/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.version/0","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.version() |> Version.parse!()\n    iex> :ok\n    :ok","ref":"Localize.Inputs.html#version/0-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Components","doc":"HEEx components for locale-aware form input.\n\nToday: `number_input/1`. More inputs (percentage, ratio,\ndimension, …) will land here over time under the same\nnamespace.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Setup - Localize.Inputs.Components","doc":"Add the JS hook in your `assets/js/app.js`:\n\n    import Hooks from \"localize_inputs\"\n    let liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n      hooks: { NumberInput: Hooks.NumberInput }\n    })\n\nInstall AutoNumeric as a peer dep:\n\n    npm install autonumeric","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#module-setup"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"Locale-aware plain-number input.\n\nRenders an ` ` wrapped\nin a ` ` that carries `data-` attributes the JS hook\nreads (locale, separators, minus sign, min/max, decimals).\nWith AutoNumeric loaded the input live-formats as the user\ntypes; without it, the server-side parser\n(`Localize.Inputs.Parser`) accepts whatever the user typed\non submit.\n\nThe form value submits as the canonical period-decimal form\non submit (e.g. `\"1234.56\"`), suitable for casting straight\ninto a `Decimal` or `:integer` Ecto field.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"* `assigns` — see the per-attribute documentation below.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Attributes - Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"* `:form` — the `Phoenix.HTML.Form` the field belongs to.\n\n* `:field` — the form field as an atom.\n\n* `:locale` — display locale. Defaults to\n  `Localize.get_locale/0`.\n\n* `:integer` — when `true`, accept integers only and emit\n  `inputmode=\"numeric\"`.\n\n* `:min`, `:max` — value bounds.\n\n* `:decimals` — maximum fractional digits.\n\n* `:align` — `:left` (default), `:right`, or `:center`.\n\n* `:placeholder` — placeholder text.\n\n* `:js` — set to `false` to skip the `phx-hook` attribute.\n\n* `:class`, `:input_class` — extra classes for the wrapper\n  and the input.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1-attributes"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"* A `Phoenix.LiveView.Rendered` struct containing the input\n  markup.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"<.number_input form={@form} field={:quantity} integer={true} min={1} max={999} />\n    <.number_input form={@form} field={:rating} min={0} max={5} decimals={1} />","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Attributes - Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1","doc":"* `form` (`Phoenix.HTML.Form`) (required)\n* `field` (`:atom`) (required)\n* `value` (`:any`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `locale` (`:string`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `integer` (`:boolean`) - Defaults to `false`.\n* `min` (`:any`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `max` (`:any`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `decimals` (`:integer`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `align` (`:atom`) - Defaults to `:left`. Must be one of `:left`, `:right`, or `:center`.\n* `placeholder` (`:string`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `js` (`:boolean`) - Defaults to `true`.\n* `class` (`:string`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* `input_class` (`:string`) - Defaults to `nil`.\n* Global attributes are accepted. Supports all globals plus: `[\"disabled\", \"readonly\", \"required\", \"autofocus\"]`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Components.html#number_input/1-attributes-1"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset","doc":"Ecto.Changeset helpers for `Localize.Inputs`.\n\nOnly compiled when `:ecto` is loaded.\n\n    schema \"products\" do\n      field :quantity, :integer\n      field :rating,   :decimal\n    end\n\n    def changeset(product, attrs) do\n      product\n      |> Ecto.Changeset.cast(attrs, [:quantity, :rating])\n      |> Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number(:quantity, min: 1)\n      |> Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number(:rating, min: 0, max: 5, decimals: 1)\n    end","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number/3","doc":"Validates a `Decimal` / integer field with the rules from\n`Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html#validate_number/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number/3","doc":"* `changeset` is an `Ecto.Changeset.t/0`.\n\n* `field` is the field name as an atom.\n\n* `options` is a keyword list of options forwarded to\n  `Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html#validate_number/3-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number/3","doc":"* `:required` — when `true`, `nil` is rejected.\n\n* `:min` — minimum allowed value.\n\n* `:max` — maximum allowed value.\n\n* `:decimals` — maximum number of fractional digits.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html#validate_number/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number/3","doc":"* The changeset, with one error added per failing check.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html#validate_number/3-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number/3","doc":"iex> changeset = Ecto.Changeset.cast({%{}, %{quantity: :integer}}, %{\"quantity\" => 5}, [:quantity])\n    iex> changeset = Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number(changeset, :quantity, min: 1, max: 10)\n    iex> changeset.valid?\n    true","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Changeset.html#validate_number/3-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter","doc":"Server-side formatter for parsed number values.\n\nThis is the *blur* formatter — what the server renders into\nthe input's `value` attribute after a round-trip when the JS\nhook isn't active (Path A fallback) or for the initial server\nrender. Live, as-you-type formatting is the JS hook's job.\n\nDelegates to `Localize.Number.to_string/2`; this module does\nno formatting of its own.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number/2","doc":"Formats a parsed value for display in a number input.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html#format_number/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number/2","doc":"* `value` is a `Decimal`, integer, float, locale-formatted\n  string, or `nil`.\n\n* `options` is a keyword list of options.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html#format_number/2-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number/2","doc":"* `:locale` — the locale to format under. Defaults to\n  `Localize.get_locale/0`.\n\n* All other options are passed through to\n  `Localize.Number.to_string/2`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html#format_number/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number/2","doc":"* The locale-formatted string.\n\n* `\"\"` when the value is `nil` or empty.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html#format_number/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number/2","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number(Decimal.new(\"1234.56\"), locale: :en)\n    \"1,234.56\"\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number(Decimal.new(\"1234.56\"), locale: :de)\n    \"1.234,56\"\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number(nil)\n    \"\"","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Formatter.html#format_number/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Locale","doc":"Locale-derived display data for number form inputs.\n\nReturns the decimal/grouping separator characters, the native\ndigit system, and the locale's minus sign — everything a JS\nhook needs to render a number in the user's locale.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.t/0","doc":"Display data for a locale.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve/2","doc":"Resolves display data (separators, digit system, minus sign)\nfor a locale.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html#resolve/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve/2","doc":"* `locale` is a locale identifier (atom, string, or\n  `Localize.LanguageTag.t/0`). Defaults to\n  `Localize.get_locale/0`.\n\n* `options` is reserved for future expansion. Unused today.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html#resolve/2-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve/2","doc":"* `{:ok, t()}` carrying the locale's display data.\n\n* `{:error, Exception.t()}` when the locale can't be resolved.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html#resolve/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve/2","doc":"iex> {:ok, info} = Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve(:en)\n    iex> info.decimal\n    \".\"\n\n    iex> {:ok, info} = Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve(:de)\n    iex> {info.decimal, info.group}\n    {\",\", \".\"}","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Locale.html#resolve/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Parser","doc":"Front-door parser for locale-aware number form input.\n\nDelegates to `Localize.Number.Parser.parse/2`. The input layer\ndoes no parsing of its own — this module is a thin policy\nlayer that adds form-input tolerance (paste artefacts,\naccounting parentheses, NBSP normalisation) before forwarding.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number/2","doc":"Parses a locale-formatted number from a user-typed string.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#parse_number/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number/2","doc":"* `string` is the raw user input.\n\n* `options` is a keyword list of options.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#parse_number/2-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number/2","doc":"* `:locale` — the locale to interpret the string under.\n  Defaults to `Localize.get_locale/0`.\n\n* `:integer` — when `true`, only integers are accepted.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#parse_number/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number/2","doc":"* `{:ok, Decimal.t()}` (or `{:ok, integer()}` when\n  `integer: true`).\n\n* `{:ok, nil}` for blank input.\n\n* `{:error, Exception.t() | {module(), String.t()}}` on parse\n  failure.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#parse_number/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number/2","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"1,234.56\", locale: :en)\n    {:ok, Decimal.new(\"1234.56\")}\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"1.234,56\", locale: :de)\n    {:ok, Decimal.new(\"1234.56\")}\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"\", locale: :en)\n    {:ok, nil}\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"(1,234.56)\", locale: :en)\n    {:ok, Decimal.new(\"-1234.56\")}","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#parse_number/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical/1","doc":"Normalises a parsed value to its canonical period-decimal\nstring form — what a JS-driven form submission expects.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#to_canonical/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical/1","doc":"* `value` is a `Decimal`, integer, or `nil`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#to_canonical/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical/1","doc":"* A binary in canonical period-decimal form.\n\n* `nil` when the input is `nil`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#to_canonical/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical/1","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical(Decimal.new(\"1234.56\"))\n    \"1234.56\"\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Parser.to_canonical(nil)\n    nil","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Parser.html#to_canonical/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Validator","doc":"Server-side validation for parsed number values.\n\nPure Elixir, no Ecto dependency. The Ecto changeset bridge is\nin `Localize.Inputs.Changeset`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.error/0","doc":"An error produced by the validator.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#t:error/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2","doc":"Validates a parsed number against bounds, precision, and\nrequired-ness.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#validate_number/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2","doc":"* `value` is a `Decimal`, integer, or `nil`.\n\n* `options` is a keyword list of options.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#validate_number/2-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2","doc":"* `:required` — when `true`, `nil` is rejected.\n\n* `:min` — minimum allowed value (any numeric form the parser\n  accepts).\n\n* `:max` — maximum allowed value.\n\n* `:decimals` — maximum number of fractional digits.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#validate_number/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2","doc":"* `:ok` when every check passes.\n\n* `{:error, [{atom(), String.t()}]}` with one entry per failing\n  check, in the order `:required`, `:min`, `:max`, `:decimals`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#validate_number/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number/2","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number(Decimal.new(\"5\"), min: 1, max: 10)\n    :ok\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number(Decimal.new(\"15\"), max: 10)\n    {:error, [{:max, \"must be at most 10\"}]}\n\n    iex> Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number(nil, required: true)\n    {:error, [{:required, \"is required\"}]}","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Validator.html#validate_number/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer","doc":"A web-based visualizer for `Localize.Inputs`.\n\n`Plug.Router` that can be mounted inside a Phoenix or Plug\napplication, or run standalone during development via\n`Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Views - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer","doc":"* `/input` — interactive number input demo.\n* `/parse` — cross-locale parsing table.\n* `/format` — cross-locale formatting table.\n* `/locale` — locale display data table.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.html#module-views"},{"type":"module","title":"Enable flag - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer","doc":"`Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1` refuses to\nboot unless `:localize_inputs, :visualizer` is set to `true`\nin config (or `enabled: true` is passed explicitly).\nMounting under `forward/2` in a Phoenix router is not gated.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.html#module-enable-flag"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.call/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.call/2 .","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.html#call/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.init/1 .","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.html#init/1"},{"type":"module","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone","doc":"Runs `Localize.Inputs.Visualizer` as a standalone Bandit\nweb server for local development.\n\n    Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start(port: 4003)\n    # Visit http://localhost:4003","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Enable flag - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone","doc":"Refuses to start unless the visualizer has been enabled:\n\n    config :localize_inputs, visualizer: true\n\nor pass `enabled: true` to `start/1` explicitly.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#module-enable-flag"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a child spec for embedding the visualizer under a\nsupervision tree.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.child_spec/1","doc":"* `options` is a keyword list of options. See `start/1`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#child_spec/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.child_spec/1","doc":"* A `Supervisor.child_spec/0`. When the visualizer is\n  disabled, a temporary no-op spec is returned instead of a\n  live listener.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#child_spec/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?/1","doc":"Returns whether the visualizer is currently enabled.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#enabled?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?/1","doc":"* `options` is a keyword list of options.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#enabled?/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?/1","doc":"* `:enabled` — pass `true` to force-enable regardless of\n  application config.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#enabled?/1-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?/1","doc":"* `true` when either the application env flag or the option\n  is set.\n\n* `false` otherwise.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#enabled?/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?/1","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.enabled?(enabled: true)\n    true","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#enabled?/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1","doc":"Starts the visualizer as a standalone Bandit web server.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#start/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1","doc":"* `options` is a keyword list of options.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#start/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1","doc":"* `:port` — TCP port. Defaults to `4003`.\n\n* `:ip` — bind address. `:loopback` (default), `:any`, or a\n  `{a, b, c, d}` IPv4 tuple.\n\n* `:enabled` — pass `true` to override the application-level\n  enable flag.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#start/1-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1","doc":"* `{:ok, pid()}` when the server starts.\n\n* `{:error, :visualizer_disabled}` when the enable flag is\n  not set.\n\n* `{:error, term()}` propagated from `Bandit.start_link/1`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#start/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start/1","doc":"iex> Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start(enabled: false)\n    {:error, :visualizer_disabled}","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#start/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.stop/1","doc":"Stops a previously-started visualizer.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#stop/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.stop/1","doc":"* `pid` is the pid returned from `start/1`.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#stop/1-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.stop/1","doc":"* `:ok` once the supervisor has shut down.","ref":"Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.html#stop/1-returns"},{"type":"extras","title":"Localize.Inputs","doc":"# Localize.Inputs\n\nLocale-aware HTML form input components. Today: `<.number_input>`. More inputs will land here over time (percentage, ratio, dimension, …).\n\nBuilt on top of [`localize`](https://hex.pm/packages/localize). Wraps [AutoNumeric](https://autonumeric.org/) for live formatting and cursor preservation.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Localize.Inputs","doc":"```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:localize_inputs, \"~> 0.1\"},\n\n    # Activate the HEEx component:\n    {:phoenix_html, \"~> 4.0\"},\n    {:phoenix_live_view, \"~> 1.0\"},\n\n    # Activate the Ecto changeset bridge:\n    {:ecto, \"~> 3.10\"},\n\n    # Activate the visualizer:\n    {:plug, \"~> 1.15\", only: :dev},\n    {:bandit, \"~> 1.5\",  only: :dev}\n  ]\nend\n```\n\nThe `phoenix_html`, `phoenix_live_view`, `ecto`, `plug`, `bandit` and `gettext` deps are all optional — the headless parser/formatter/validator compile without any of them. Each layer activates when its dep is present.","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Layered API - Localize.Inputs","doc":"","ref":"readme.html#layered-api"},{"type":"extras","title":"Headless (no Phoenix dependency) - Localize.Inputs","doc":"```elixir\n{:ok, %Decimal{} = decimal} = Localize.Inputs.Parser.parse_number(\"1.234,56\", locale: :de)\n\nLocalize.Inputs.Formatter.format_number(decimal, locale: :en)\n#=> \"1,234.56\"\n\n:ok = Localize.Inputs.Validator.validate_number(decimal, min: 0)\n\n{:ok, info} = Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve(:de)\ninfo.decimal   #=> \",\"\ninfo.group     #=> \".\"\n```","ref":"readme.html#headless-no-phoenix-dependency"},{"type":"extras","title":"Ecto changeset - Localize.Inputs","doc":"```elixir\nchangeset\n|> Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number(:quantity, min: 1, max: 999)\n|> Localize.Inputs.Changeset.validate_number(:rating,   min: 0, max: 5, decimals: 1)\n```","ref":"readme.html#ecto-changeset"},{"type":"extras","title":"HEEx component - Localize.Inputs","doc":"```heex\n<.number_input form={@form} field={:quantity} integer={true} min={1} max={999} />\n<.number_input form={@form} field={:rating}   min={0} max={5} decimals={1} />\n```\n\nImport the component via `import Localize.Inputs.Components` in your view module.","ref":"readme.html#heex-component"},{"type":"extras","title":"JS hook (AutoNumeric) - Localize.Inputs","doc":"Install AutoNumeric as a peer dependency:\n\n```bash\nnpm install autonumeric\n```\n\nIn `assets/js/app.js`:\n\n```javascript\nimport AutoNumeric from \"autonumeric\"\nimport Hooks from \"localize_inputs\"\n\nHooks.configure({ AutoNumeric })\n\nnew LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n  hooks: { NumberInput: Hooks.NumberInput }\n})\n```\n\nWithout AutoNumeric loaded the input still works — the server-side parser accepts whatever the user typed on submit. Live formatting and cursor preservation are off in that fallback.","ref":"readme.html#js-hook-autonumeric"},{"type":"extras","title":"Visualizer - Localize.Inputs","doc":"A Plug-based development tool that demos the component across CLDR locales with a light/dark theme toggle. Refuses to start unless the enable flag is set:\n\n```elixir\n# In config/dev.exs:\nconfig :localize_inputs, visualizer: true\n\n# Standalone (zero-config):\n{:ok, _pid} = Localize.Inputs.Visualizer.Standalone.start(port: 4003)\n\n# Or mount into a host Phoenix app:\nforward \"/inputs\", Localize.Inputs.Visualizer\n```\n\nTabs:\n\n* **`/input`** — interactive `<.number_input>` demo with locale + AutoNumeric mounted.\n* **`/parse`** — same input, every locale, side-by-side (separator inversion, paste tolerance).\n* **`/format`** — same parsed value, every locale.\n* **`/locale`** — the `Localize.Inputs.Locale.resolve/1` snapshot per locale.","ref":"readme.html#visualizer"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Localize.Inputs","doc":"Apache-2.0. See [`LICENSE.md`](LICENSE.md).","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"v0.1.0 (initial release) - Changelog","doc":"* `Localize.Inputs.Components.number_input/1` — locale-aware plain-number HEEx component backed by an AutoNumeric JS hook, with a headless parser/formatter/validator and Ecto changeset bridge.\n\n* `Localize.Inputs.Visualizer` — Plug-based development tool with light/dark theme toggle that demonstrates the component across CLDR locales.","ref":"changelog.html#v0-1-0-initial-release"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"# License\n\nCopyright 2026 Kip Cole\n\nLicensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in\ncompliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the License at\n\n    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n\nUnless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License\nis distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or\nimplied. See the License for the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the\nLicense.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.2"}}